window.T19_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"bead – dramatic","cards":[{"w":"bead","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of glass, wood, or other material, pierced for stringing","c":"念珠；小珠子；水珠（可數）","s":"The creative young girl loved to string colorful glass beads together to make pretty bracelets for her friends.","t":"那位富有創意的小女孩喜歡把五顏六色的玻璃珠子串在一起，為朋友們製作漂亮的手環。"},{"w":"bride","p":"n.","d":"a woman on her wedding day or just before or after the event","c":"新娘；即將結婚的女子（可數）","s":"The beautiful bride looked radiant in her elegant white lace gown as she walked down the church aisle.","t":"美麗的新娘身穿優雅的白蕾絲禮服，走在教堂走道上時顯得光彩照人。"},{"w":"casual","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and unconcerned; not formal; happening by chance","c":"休閒的；非正式的；漫不經心的；偶然的","s":"Because our modern technology company has a relaxed dress code, all software engineers can wear comfortable casual clothes to the office.","t":"因為我們這家現代科技公司有寬鬆的穿著規範，所有軟體工程師都可以穿著舒適的休閒服飾上班。"},{"w":"column","p":"n.","d":"an upright pillar; a vertical division of a page; a regular article in a paper","c":"石柱；柱狀物；（報紙）專欄；縱列（可數）","s":"The ancient Greek temple on top of the windy hill is supported by twenty magnificent marble columns.","t":"山頂上的古希臘神廟由二十根壯麗的大理石石柱／圓柱所支撐。"},{"w":"crop","p":"n.","d":"a cultivated plant that is grown as food on a large scale","c":"農作物；收成（可數/不可數）","s":"Due to the continuous drought that lasted for three months, farmers in the southern valley suffered severe crop failure.","t":"由於持續了三個月的乾旱，南部山谷的農民遭受了嚴重的作物歉收。"},{"w":"crop","p":"v.","d":"to harvest or cut off; to appear unexpectedly (crop up)","c":"收割；修剪；剪裁（照片）；突然出現（動詞）","s":"We were ready to leave the office on Friday afternoon when an urgent technical problem suddenly cropped up.","t":"我們週五下午正準備離開辦公室，這時一個緊急的技術問題卻突然出乎意料地冒出來。"},{"w":"dime","p":"n.","d":"a ten-cent coin in the US and Canada","c":"（美、加的一角硬幣，值十美分）（可數）","s":"In modern consumer societies, cheap plastic toys produced by automated factories are practically a dime a dozen in every toy store.","t":"在現代消費社會中，自動化工廠生產的廉價塑膠玩具在每家玩具店裡簡直到處都是／多得不值錢。"},{"w":"dirt","p":"n.","d":"loose soil or earth; unclean matter that soils someone or something","c":"泥土；塵垢；污垢（不可數）","s":"After playing football outside in the pouring rain, the boys returned home with their uniforms covered in dirt.","t":"在傾盆大雨中踢完足球後，男孩們穿著滿是泥垢的球衣回到家中。"},{"w":"dramatic","p":"adj.","d":"relating to drama or the theater; sudden, striking, and exciting","c":"戲劇性的；引人注目的；急劇的","s":"The popular actress loved to make a dramatic entrance at glamorous film festivals by wearing a sparkling red gown.","t":"這位受歡迎的女演員喜歡在光彩奪目的電影節上穿著閃亮的紅色禮服引人注目地登場。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"familiar – gum","cards":[{"w":"familiar","p":"adj.","d":"well known from long or close association; easily recognized","c":"熟悉的；熟知的；常見的","s":"Our new office manager is very familiar with the complicated digital software used for tracking inventory.","t":"我們的新辦公室經理非常熟悉用於追蹤庫存的複雜數位軟體。"},{"w":"frank","p":"adj.","d":"open, honest, and direct in speech or writing","c":"坦白的；直率的；真誠的","s":"To be frank, I do not believe that their ambitious business plan will succeed without substantial outside investment.","t":"坦白說，如果沒有大量的外部投資，我不認為他們雄心勃勃的商業計劃會成功。"},{"w":"fright","p":"n.","d":"a sudden intense feeling of fear or shock","c":"驚嚇；恐懼；驚恐（不可數/可數）","s":"When the loud thunder roared right above the house, the sudden noise gave the sleeping baby a terrible fright.","t":"當響雷在房屋正上方轟鳴時，突如其來的巨響把熟睡中的嬰兒嚇了一大跳。"},{"w":"fuel","p":"n.","d":"material such as coal, gas, or oil burned to produce heat or power","c":"燃料；提供力量的來源（不可數/可數）","s":"Burning excessive amounts of fossil fuels has significantly contributed to severe global warming and climate change worldwide.","t":"燃燒過量的化石燃料在全球範圍內顯著加劇了嚴重的全球暖化與氣候變遷。"},{"w":"fuel","p":"v.","d":"to supply with fuel; to sustain or inflame an emotion or argument","c":"為…添加燃料；激起；刺激；推動（動詞）","s":"Rapid advances in artificial intelligence and automation continue to fuel strong economic growth across the tech sector.","t":"人工智慧與自動化的快速發展繼續推動整個科技領域強勁的經濟成長。"},{"w":"gamble","p":"v.","d":"to play games of chance for money; to take risky actions in hope of success","c":"賭博；冒險；孤注一擲（動詞）","s":"The foolish young man went to the casino and tragically gambled away his entire monthly salary in one evening.","t":"那個愚蠢的年輕人去賭場，在一晚之內悲劇性地把他的全部月薪在賭博中輸光。"},{"w":"gamble","p":"n.","d":"an act of gambling; a risky undertaking with an uncertain outcome","c":"賭博；投機；高風險的冒險嘗試（可數）","s":"Leaving a secure corporate job to open a boutique bakery was a huge gamble, but it paid off handsomely.","t":"離開一份穩定的企業工作去開一家精品烘焙坊是一個巨大的冒險嘗試，但它帶來了豐厚的回報。"},{"w":"greedy","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing an intense and selfish desire for wealth, power, or food","c":"貪婪的；貪心的；渴望更多的","s":"The corrupt corporation was so greedy for profits that it completely ignored basic environmental safety regulations.","t":"這家腐敗的企業如此貪求利潤，以至於徹底無視基本的環境安全法規。"},{"w":"grocery","p":"n.","d":"a grocer's store; food and household goods sold by a grocer (groceries)","c":"雜貨店；食品雜貨（常用複數 groceries）（可數）","s":"Every Saturday morning, my parents drive to the local grocery store to purchase fresh fruits and vegetables.","t":"每週六早晨，我的父母開車前往當地的食品雜貨店採買新鮮的水果與蔬菜。"},{"w":"gum","p":"n.","d":"chewing gum; the firm pink flesh around the roots of the teeth","c":"口香糖（不可數）；牙齦；齒齦（常用複數 gums）","s":"The polite school rule strictly forbids students from chewing sweet bubble gum during formal classroom lectures.","t":"校規禮貌而嚴格地禁止學生在正式課堂演講期間咀嚼甜甜的泡泡糖／口香糖。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"hairdresser – maid","cards":[{"w":"hairdresser","p":"n.","d":"a person whose occupation is to cut, style, and care for hair","c":"美髮師；美髮造型師（可數）","s":"Before attending her sister's grand wedding banquet, Olivia booked an appointment with a talented hairdresser to style her hair.","t":"在參加姐姐盛大的婚宴之前，奧莉薇亞預約了一位才華洋溢的美髮師為她做造型。"},{"w":"hallway","p":"n.","d":"an interior passage or corridor onto which rooms open","c":"走廊；門廳；玄關（可數）","s":"Students are strictly instructed not to run or shout loudly down the narrow hallway between classes.","t":"學生們受到嚴格告誡，下課時間不得在狹窄的走廊上奔跑或大聲喊叫。"},{"w":"hammer","p":"n.","d":"a tool with a heavy metal head used for pounding or driving nails","c":"鐵鎚；槌子（可數）","s":"The careful carpenter used a sturdy claw hammer and several long nails to repair the broken wooden fence.","t":"細心的木匠使用堅固的羊角鐵鎚和幾根長釘子修理了損壞的木籬笆。"},{"w":"hammer","p":"v.","d":"to hit or beat with a hammer; to work hard to reach an agreement","c":"槌打；敲擊；擊敗；歷經艱辛達成（動詞）","s":"Diplomats from both rival nations worked through the night to successfully hammer out a peaceful trade agreement.","t":"來自兩個競爭國家的外交官徹夜工作，成功艱難達成了和平貿易協議。"},{"w":"heal","p":"v.","d":"to cause a wound or injury to become healthy again; to cure","c":"（傷口、情感）癒合；治癒；恢復（動詞）","s":"Although the sudden breakup was deeply painful, her caring grandmother reminded her that time heals all wounds eventually.","t":"雖然突然的分手極為痛苦，但慈祥的祖母提醒她，時間最終會治癒所有的創傷。"},{"w":"lord","p":"n.","d":"a person of noble rank or high authority; God or Christ (the Lord)","c":"貴族；領主；統治者；主／上帝（可數）","s":"During the European Middle Ages, peasants were required to work the land and pay heavy taxes to their local feudal lord.","t":"在歐洲中世紀，農民被要求耕種土地並向當地的封建領主繳納沉重的賦稅。"},{"w":"loser","p":"n.","d":"a person or team that loses a contest or game; an unsuccessful person","c":"輸家；失敗者（可數）","s":"Even though his basketball team was defeated in the finals, Tom shook hands with his opponents like a good loser.","t":"儘管他的籃球隊在決賽中落敗，提姆依然像個有風度的輸家一樣與對手握手。"},{"w":"lung","p":"n.","d":"either of the two breathing organs situated within the chest cavity","c":"肺；肺臟（可數，常用複數 lungs）","s":"Medical doctors around the world strongly emphasize that smoking cigarettes significantly increases the dangerous risk of developing lung cancer.","t":"世界各地的醫學專家強烈強調，吸菸會顯著增加罹患肺癌的危險性。"},{"w":"maid","p":"n.","d":"a female domestic servant, especially in a hotel or large house","c":"女僕；侍女；飯店客房清潔員（可數）","s":"Every morning, the hardworking hotel maid replaces the towels and makes sure the guest rooms are spotless.","t":"每天早晨，勤奮的飯店客房清潔女僕會更換毛巾並確保客房一塵不染。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"marker – spice","cards":[{"w":"marker","p":"n.","d":"a felt-tip pen; an object used to indicate a position or boundary","c":"彩色彩色筆；白板筆；標誌物；指示物（可數）","s":"The creative teacher used a bright red whiteboard marker to underline important grammar rules on the board.","t":"富有創意的老師使用一支鮮紅色的白板麥克筆，在白板上劃線強調重要的文法規則。"},{"w":"meadow","p":"n.","d":"a piece of grassland, especially one used for hay or grazing","c":"草地；牧草地（可數）","s":"During warm spring afternoons, herds of gentle cows grazed peacefully across the green grassy meadow.","t":"在溫暖的春日下午，成群溫馴的乳牛在綠意盎然的青草地上平靜地吃草。"},{"w":"microphone","p":"n.","d":"an instrument for converting sound waves into electrical energy variations","c":"麥克風；話筒（可數）","s":"Before beginning her keynote lecture to the large auditorium, the speaker tapped the wireless microphone to test the volume.","t":"在向大禮堂發表主題演講之前，講者輕敲了無線麥克風以測試音量。"},{"w":"pass","p":"n.","d":"an official document or ticket permitting entrance or travel; a narrow route","c":"通行證；入場券；合格；山隘（可數）","s":"International airline passengers must present both their valid passports and printed boarding passes before entering the departure gate.","t":"國際航班乘客在進入登機門前，必須同時出示有效護照和列印好的登機證。"},{"w":"pass","p":"v.","d":"to move past; to succeed in an exam; to transfer something to someone","c":"通過；穿過；傳遞；（考試）及格（動詞）","s":"After studying diligently for weeks, Lucy was thrilled to learn that she had passed the difficult national certification exam.","t":"在勤奮學習數週後，露西得知自己通過了／考過了艱難的國家證照考試，感到無比興奮。"},{"w":"poverty","p":"n.","d":"the state of being extremely poor; insufficiency","c":"貧窮；貧困；匱乏（不可數）","s":"Millions of disadvantaged children living in rural developing regions still live in extreme poverty without access to clean water.","t":"生活在農村開發中地區的數百萬弱勢兒童仍然生活在極度貧困中，無法獲得乾淨的飲用水。"},{"w":"profit","p":"n.","d":"a financial gain, especially the difference between the amount earned and spent","c":"利潤；收益；贏利（可數/不可數）","s":"By reducing unnecessary operating costs, the retail company managed to make a handsome profit during the holiday season.","t":"透過降低不必要的營運成本，這家零售公司成功在假期季節賺取了可觀的利潤。"},{"w":"profit","p":"v.","d":"to obtain a financial advantage or benefit; to gain advantage","c":"獲利；獲益；受惠（動詞）","s":"Savvy investors who understood renewable technology early profited greatly from the global transition to green energy.","t":"早期理解可再生技術的精明投資者，從全球轉向綠色能源的過程中獲利豐厚。"},{"w":"scatter","p":"v.","d":"to throw in various random directions; to disperse or cause to separate","c":"散播；散開；驅散；散落（動詞）","s":"In early spring, the organic farmer walked across the cultivated fields to evenly scatter wheat seeds into the rich soil.","t":"在早春時節，有機農民走過耕作過的田地，將小麥種子均勻地播撒進肥沃的土壤中。"},{"w":"spice","p":"n.","d":"an aromatic vegetable substance used to flavor food; interesting excitement","c":"香料；調味品（可數/不可數）；情趣；趣味","s":"Indian cooking is world-famous because chefs skillfully blend dozens of fragrant spices and herbs to create delicious curries.","t":"印度料理聞名世界，因為廚師們巧妙地融合了數十種芬芳的香料與草本調味品以製作美味的咖哩。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"strategy – youngster","cards":[{"w":"strategy","p":"n.","d":"a plan of action designed to achieve a long-term or overall aim","c":"策略；戰略；計策（可數/不可數）","s":"The head coach developed an aggressive winning strategy to beat their fierce rivals in the championship game.","t":"總教練制定了一項進攻性的致勝策略，以在冠軍爭奪戰中擊敗強勁的對手。"},{"w":"sum","p":"n.","d":"a particular amount of money; the total amount resulting from the addition","c":"金額；總數；總和（可數）","s":"The generous philanthropist donated a large sum of money to build modern computer libraries for rural elementary schools.","t":"那位慷慨的慈善家捐贈了一大筆錢，為偏鄉小學建造現代化的電腦圖書館。"},{"w":"sum","p":"v.","d":"to calculate the total of; to summarize the main points (sum up)","c":"總結；概括（常與 up 連用）；加總（動詞）","s":"At the conclusion of the ninety-minute lecture, the professor took five minutes to concisely sum up the main points.","t":"在九十分鐘演講結束時，教授花了五分鐘簡明扼要地總結了重點。"},{"w":"survivor","p":"n.","d":"a person who survives a disaster, accident, or serious illness","c":"生還者；倖存者（可數）","s":"Brave rescue workers worked around the clock through the rubble to pull three miraculous earthquake survivors from the ruins.","t":"勇敢的救援人員日以繼夜地在瓦礫堆中工作，從廢墟中救出了三名奇蹟般的地震生還者。"},{"w":"swell","p":"v.","d":"to become larger or rounder in size; to increase in volume or intensity","c":"腫脹；膨脹；增加；（情感）湧上心頭（動詞）","s":"After Jerry accidentally twisted his left ankle during the basketball match, his foot immediately began to swell up painfully.","t":"在傑瑞在籃球比賽中不小心扭傷左腳踝後，他的腳立刻開始劇痛並腫脹起來。"},{"w":"temporary","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for only a limited period of time; not permanent","c":"暫時的；臨時的；短暫的","s":"Following the devastating tropical typhoon, emergency government workers set up temporary shelters with clean water and blankets for displaced villagers.","t":"在毀滅性的熱帶颱風過後，緊急政府工作人員為無家可歸的村民設立了提供乾淨飲用水與毛毯的臨時避難所。"},{"w":"visible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be seen; noticeable or clear","c":"顯而易見的；看得見的；引人注目的","s":"During crisp winter nights far away from city light pollution, thousands of sparkling stars are clearly visible across the sky.","t":"在遠離城市光害的涼爽冬夜裡，數千顆閃爍的繁星在夜空中清晰可見。"},{"w":"youngster","p":"n.","d":"a child, young person, or youth","c":"年輕人；少年；兒童（可數）","s":"The community sports center organized a summer soccer clinic to encourage energetic youngsters to exercise outdoors regularly.","t":"社區體育中心組織了一個夏季足球訓練營，以鼓勵精力充沛的年輕人／學童定期在戶外運動。"}]}];
